      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(a) With δεῖ, the person who ‘must’ goes into the acc. case, e.g.\n    δεῖ με/σε/αὐτοὺς ἰέναι ‘it is necessary for me/you/them/ to go’, ‘I/you/they must go’\n(b) With ἀνάγκη ἐστί, the person for whom it is obligatory goes into the acc. case (or sometimes the dat.), e.g.\n    ἀνάγκη ἐστὶ τὸν θεὸν/ὑμᾶς λέγειν      lit. ‘It is obligatory for the god/you to speak’ or\n    ἀνάγκη ἐστὶ τῷ θεῷ/ὑμῖν λέγειν\n    i.e. ‘The god is/you are obliged to speak’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
