      "margin_number": "155",
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The big giveaway with comparatives and superlatives is the -τερος -τατος\nendings. But should that be -ωτερος or -οτερος, -ωτατος or -οτατος? Learn\nthe usual rules for the formation of the comp. and sup. adjectives:",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 155,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        195,
        822,
        916,
        916
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(a) Short vowel stem: σοφ-\nUsually, when the last syllable of the adjective’s stem is short (i.e. contains a\nsingle short vowel as in σοφ-ός), -ώτερος and -ώτατος are added to form the\ncomparative and superlative adjectives, e.g. σοφώτερος and σοφώτατος.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
